WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
Welcome to Cloud Minute

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.800
Let's take a look at how to upload files and folders to Google Cloud Storage

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.220
First, go to the Storage Browser and select your Bucket.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.420
You can click "Upload Files" to select files and folder from your file picker

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.660
But my favorite is the "Drag and Drop" feature.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.760
Here, you can just Drag and Drop files and folders straight into the Web UI.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.277
Now let's open a command line in the folder with the files we want to upload

00:00:22.277 --> 00:00:25.976
I want to upload "file2.txt" and "folder2" to Cloud Storage

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.320
To upload "file2.txt", type in

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:36.800
'gsutil', then 'cp', then the name of the file 'file2.txt', and finally the name of the Cloud Storage bucket 'gs://temporal-loop-94520'

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.918
If we refresh our Google Developer Console, we can see that the new file has been uploaded

00:00:40.918 --> 00:00:42.572
Now let's copy 'folder2'

00:00:42.572 --> 00:00:52.012
Type in 'gsutil' then '-m' for multicore, then 'cp' then '-r' for recursive, then the name of the folder 'folder2' then the name of the bucket 'gs://temporal-loop-94520'

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.880
If we refresh our Google Developer Console, we can see the new folder with all the files inside of it!

